the built-in definitions, so a supplied formula with the same name
takes precedence. Use unique names within \code{molecular_formula}.

For each candidate, component formulas are multiplied by their
counts using \code{\link[enviPat:multiform]{enviPat::multiform()}} and combined using
\code{\link[enviPat:mergeform]{enviPat::mergeform()}}. Components with zero counts are skipped.
The assembled formula is processed by \code{\link[enviPat:check_chemform]{enviPat::check_chemform()}}.

Formulas describe each component's contribution to the complete
candidate formula. No additional water or reducing-end correction
is added. Custom formulas should be consistent with the mass
contributions used to construct the glycan library; this consistency
is not checked by the function.

The theoretical isotope pattern is calculated using the candidate's
\code{charge_state}, the isotope data supplied by enviPat, and
\code{rel_to = 2}. Formula-based isotope calculation does not use the
stored \code{neutral_monoisotopic_mass} to construct the pattern.
